<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="/sitemap.xsl"?>
<!--
  Codivio sitemap (Phase 3.1; updated for the Phase 4.9 SEO follow-up,
  Phase 3.18 HTML Site Map, and Phase 3.18's XSLT visual-design follow-up).

  The <?xml-stylesheet?> line above is presentation-only: a browser that
  opens this URL directly renders it via public/sitemap.xsl + sitemap.css
  (Codivio-branded HTML view). Search engines ignore this instruction and
  read the urlset/url structure below exactly as before — the file
  remains valid XML per the sitemaps.org schema, unchanged in every way
  that matters for crawling. See public/sitemap.xsl's own header comment
  for why the styling is a linked file rather than inline (CSP).

  Lists only real, currently indexable public pages. As of the Phase 4.9
  follow-up, 2 of the 34 tool pages — QR Code Generator and QR Code
  Scanner — have shipped real functionality (see shared/seo/tools.ts,
  whose robots entries for these two flipped to index,follow) and are
  listed below. The remaining 32 tool pages stay excluded: every one of
  them is still noindex today because ToolPage.tsx renders a "coming soon"
  placeholder, not real functionality; a sitemap should only list pages
  meant to be indexed. Update this file again when another tool ships real
  functionality and its shared/seo/tools.ts robots entry flips to
  index,follow.

  Phase 3.18 adds /sitemap itself — the real, index,follow, human-readable
  HTML directory of every page/tool (see shared/seo/pages.ts's PAGE_SEO.sitemap
  and src/App.tsx's SitemapPage) — at the same priority tier as /faq and
  /pricing (0.5/monthly): a useful secondary navigation page, not core like
  the homepage or the tools hub.

  Static (not worker-generated) for now, matching robots.txt/llms.txt —
  see DECISIONS.md's "SEO Metadata Architecture" entry for why a dynamic,
  D1-driven sitemap is future work rather than being built here.
-->
